before they hijacked those airplanes on  9 11 20 years ago tomorrow osama bin  laden's terrorists made multiple visits  to las vegas and two decades later we  still don't know for sure why they were  here george knapp the i-team has our  story  it occurred to you that we could be a  target  well we who knew i mean you know we  there were still planes flying when we  were having this decision they had made  the grounding but they hadn't all landed  yet former sheriff jerry keller says  there had been almost no discussion of  las vegas as a possible target for  attack by the likes of al qaeda prior to  the events of 9 11. but in the hectic  hours after the hijackings keller and  the other agency heads who gathered at  fbi headquarters started thinking the  unthinkable at that time i mean  terrorism  was thought to be a foreign state issue  within days local anxieties increased as  the fbi shared classified information  with keller including details still not  widely known these guys were here there  were a couple of other things there was  a a guy that  they tracked in arizona you know that  was planning to come across the dam  so you know there was nothing never  happened from that but that was early  information ringleader muhammad ara and  at least four of the other 19 hijackers  made six visits to las vegas between  late may and mid-august atta who piloted  the first plane into the world trade  center flew to las vegas on june 28  rented a car then spent 90 minutes  online in an internet cafe across from  unlv he checked into the econo lodge on  las vegas boulevard within shouting  distance of the fbi office put a do not  disturb sign on his door and stayed two  nights in a room that faced the  stratosphere tower when he returned his  rental car on july 1st it had 110 miles  on it don't know where don't know where  it i mean it does raise the central  scariest question that there might be  somebody here that helped them met with  them absolutely without a doubt  but chances are  um  i'm guessing that whoever was here  also came here from somewhere else and  they met up we just didn't ever figure  out who they were at the time future  sheriff bill young was in charge of  special ops teams for metro his  detectives and fbi agents poured through  mountains of hotel records rental car  receipts and surveillance videos to  document the terrorist movements  tipsters say at least one terrorist  received lap dances at olympic garden  others sipped coffee across from unlv  partied and gambled at casinos many  leads from the public could not be  confirmed the biggest questions remain  unanswered were they  pre-operational planning for something  here in las vegas gathering intel  were they here to plan operations  elsewhere  were they here to have their last hurrah  before they go get their  72 versions or virgins or whatever they  get and you know i'm i'm not sure  and i don't think anybody can  definitively say the hijackers weren't  the only visitors of note that summer on  9 11 itself more than a hundred members  of the saudi royal family and their  friends the bin ladens were staying in  las vegas mostly at caesar's palace and  the four seasons osama bin laden's  sister was well known at the bellagio  the saudis were grounded along with  everyone else but after being  interviewed by the fbi days later were  cleared to leave aboard three special  charter flights they were here they were  they're always here  they've been here since some of them are  gamblers  high rollers good customers  in the 20 years since 9 11 police in las  vegas and elsewhere have undergone vast  changes in how to prepare for and  respond to possible terrorist attacks  metro has greatly enhanced its own  intelligence capabilities what's also  changed is the nature of the threat  homegrown domestic terrorists are as  much or more of a threat as the foreign  variety says sheriff joe lombardo the  paradigm has changed a lot george over  the years since 9 11 you know the crux  was foreign terrorism  and then now the proliferation of  like-minded groups via the internet and  other social media spaces uh come  together and domestic terrorism has  become readily prevalent in the law  enforcement and terrorism space george  knapp 8 news now  and you can watch more of our full  interview with sheriff lombardo about  the aftermath of 9 11 on our website at  8newsnow.com brian
 

